---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { identity } from '../data/identity';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Adrian Rusu"
  description="How adrianrusu.dev uses Cloudflare Web Analytics and optional Google Analytics, including consent controls and privacy information."
>
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <span class="eyebrow">PRIVACY INFORMATION</span>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="intro-description">
      This portfolio has no advertising. I do not sell visitor information.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="section container privacy-content">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Controller and contact details</h2>
      <p>
        Adrian Rusu operates this site and is responsible for its personal-data processing. Contact: <a
          href={`mailto:${identity.email}`}>{identity.email}</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics used on this site</h2>
      <h3>Cloudflare Web Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        One manual beacon measures aggregate traffic and real-user page performance through
        <a
          href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/about/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a
        >. It runs separately from optional Google Analytics: declining Google Analytics does not
        disable it.
      </p>
      <h3>Optional Google Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        Google Analytics loads only after you choose “Allow analytics”; declining keeps the Google
        tag unloaded. Advertising storage, advertising personalization and Google Signals stay
        disabled. See <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s privacy policy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>What Google Analytics measures</h2>
      <p>
        With permission, Google Analytics uses first-party cookies to measure page views, traffic
        sources, device/browser information and engagement. Custom events record clicks on email,
        LinkedIn, public project source links, and links that open or download the résumé PDF. They
        exclude email message contents, full link text, URL query strings and fragments.
      </p>

      <h2>Your Google Analytics choice</h2>
      <p>
        Allow, decline or withdraw through Google Analytics settings below or in the footer. Your
        preference stays in this browser until you change it or clear browser storage. Withdrawal
        clears accessible Google Analytics cookies and reloads without the Google tag; it does not
        erase data already sent.
      </p>

      <h2>Other third-party resources</h2>
      <p>
        DM Sans and IBM Plex Mono load from Google Fonts, separately from your Google Analytics
        choice.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and recipients</h2>
      <p>
        Google receives Google Analytics data. This property’s event-data retention is set to two
        months, with user-data retention reset on new activity. This limit does not apply to
        standard aggregated reports. Cloudflare receives Web Analytics data; its <a
          href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/faq/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">documentation</a
        >
        describes seven days of unsampled data and access to reports for the previous six months.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where applicable, you may request access, correction, erasure, restriction or portability of
        personal data, object to processing, and withdraw consent. Contact <a
          href={`mailto:${identity.email}`}>{identity.email}</a
        >. You may also complain to a competent data-protection authority, including Romania’s
        <a
          href="https://www.dataprotection.ro/?lang=ro&page=Plangeri_meniu"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">ANSPDCP</a
        >.
      </p>
      <button
        class="privacy-settings"
        type="button"
        data-analytics-settings
        aria-controls="analytics-consent"
        aria-expanded="false">Google Analytics settings</button
      >
      <noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled, so Google Analytics does not load.</p></noscript>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .privacy-content {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .privacy-settings {
    padding: 0.65rem 1rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-light);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--surface);
    cursor: pointer;
    margin-block: 1rem;
  }
</style>
